I had a long discussion with Rast on this issue (note its listed first
in the second group). There are lots of methods to get levitation and
there are advantages / disadvantages to each. For example, I prefer a
blessed potion (guarantee > 250 turns and can end at will) for the
Plane of Air since it doesn't weigh too much (in the BoH) until use and
keeps both the boot (speed) & ring slots (free action, conflict) open
for other uses.

Earlier in the game (before reflection), I prefer NOT using rings due
to the 2% (at MC3) or more chance of destruction from lightning. I had
a wizard lose way too much stuff at the Fort within the last year
(including levitation) that I don't want to recommend it too strongly
to others at this point. In that case, I prefer boots (jumping,
levitation, or water walking) for crossing water.

Its issues like those that moved it out of the top category. [plus I
tried to keep that first list short]

